cords'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1162, 'title': 'Review and Check in Materials'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1163, 'title': 'Review Completed Materials in the field'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1164, 'title': 'Review Completed Materials in the SCO'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1165, 'title': 'Review and Check-in by the Clerk'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1166, 'title': 'Review of the SC-116, Special Census Group Quarters Control Record and SC-Q-GE, Individual Census Questionnaires'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1167, 'title': 'Item 1: All ICQs are original, not photocopies'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1168, 'title': 'Item 2: All ICQs have the GQ Case ID written on the back of the form'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1169, 'title': 'Item 3: The number of ICQs received for this GQ matches the Total Pop number written on the Control Record.'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1170, 'title': 'Item 4: The Date Enumeration Completed box is filled in (Section C, Item 30 on the SC-116).'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1171, 'title': 'Item 5: If the number of ICQs is 0 (zero) or this GQ has incomplete ICQs, then there is documentation in the Notes section of the Control Record or an accompanying SC-225, INFO-COMM.'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1172, 'title': 'Item 6: If the number of ICQs is 0 (zero) then there is a box marked in the *For Supervisory Use Only* section.'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1173, 'title': 'Corrected and Error Free Control Records'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1174, 'title': 'Reinterview'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1175, 'title': 'Transitory Locations Advance Contact (TLAC) and Enumeration at Transitory Locations (ETL)'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1176, 'title': 'What is TLAC?'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1177, 'title': 'Transitory Locations (TLs) Defined'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1178, 'title': 'Transitory Units (TUs*)*'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1179, 'title': 'A TL consists of Sites, Slips, Pads, Spaces, Rooms, or Units'}, {'children': [], 'id': 1180, 'title': 'Special Census Office (SCO) Staff Duties'}, {'childre